byid['CL-SA19-216']['statement']='Let A be a complete normal noetherian local ring of dimension two with algebraically closed residue field k and a chosen coefficient field k⊂A. Suppose X=Spec A admits a proper birational regular resolution X′, isomorphic over U=X−{closed point}. In the local Picard construction of Brauer III §8.4, NS(U) is the finite cokernel of the exceptional intersection matrix Q. Its symmetric pairing is xᵀQ⁻¹y mod ℤ. These complete hypotheses were recovered from published p.148, not invented from the isolated sheet.'
byid['CL-SA19-218']['fate']='Directly read Brauer III §8.4, pp.148–150, including (8.13)–(8.18). The omitted hypotheses are now recovered. The publication cites [9, exp.4] for connected commutative-group structure; its bibliography is unrelated to scan28.'
byid['CL-SA19-219']['fate']='Directly read Brauer III §8.1, pp.143–145, (8.1)–(8.6). The finiteness assumptions on H^(i−1)(X,μ_ell) and H^i(X,μ_ell), and the finite-cotype torsion convention, appear on printed p.144.'
byid['CL-SA19-220']['fate']='Directly read Brauer III §8.2, p.145, (8.7), with exactly the stated Picard/NS and H² finiteness assumptions. The printed page matches the reused source sheet; it cites Brauer II §3.1.'
byid['CL-SA19-221']['fate']='Directly read and visually checked Brauer III §§8.2–8.3, pp.145–147. The printed (8.8)–(8.12) also suppress the ℓ-primary component of the Brauer quotient, while NS(X)(ℓ) is explicit. This is a notation qualification of the printed text, not a manuscript transcription repair.'
byid['CL-SA19-222']['fate']='Directly read and visually checked Brauer III §8.4 p.150 and Remark 8.5 p.151. The author explicitly says he did not perform the mutual-annihilator and pairing-compatibility verification. Thus publication preserves the gap. It initially uses char k=0 for local duality and identifies cohomological purity as the obstacle to removing that condition. Targeted later-literature searches are recorded separately; no later exact completion is asserted without a matched proof.'
byid['CL-SA19-222']['fate_date']='Gap explicitly preserved in the 1968 publication; text circulated March 1966. Exact later completion not identified in this run.'
byid['CL-SA19-222']['present_status']='As of 19 November 2026: a precisely located historical proof gap, not a claim that the comparison is still an open theorem today. Elementary lattice verification alone does not settle it; the searched sources did not supply a directly matched later completion.'
