# Final direct reading: distinguish unramified quotients from étale algebras.
byid['CL-SA19-278']['statement']='At an unramified finite-type point, a principal neighborhood is a quotient of a standard étale algebra A[T]_g/(F), with F monic and F′ invertible. In the étale case, suitable localizations give the standard étale algebra itself. In the finite unramified proof, a monogenic subalgebra A[x] has the same indicated local ring as B and there is a monic relation with derivative invertible there; the kernel need not be generated by that relation. The source’s term minimal polynomial over arbitrary A requires the missing chapter context. Local monogenicity does not imply global monogenicity.'
byid['CL-SA19-278']['computation']='Read the full proof of Stacks10.152.1(0G1D), including finite reduction, the residue-field primitive element, Nakayama local isomorphism for A[x], and construction of a monic relation with invertible derivative. Compared41.12.1(025B) for the étale case and41.17.3(04HJ) for finite unramified maps. No claim that unramified implies flat.'
byid['CL-SA19-278']['fate']='The historical EGAIV4§18.4/SGA1 framework is supplemented by exact primary modern statements Stacks10.152.1(0G1D),41.12.1(025B) and41.17.3(04HJ), whose statements and indicated proofs were read. The finite unramified monogenic-subalgebra step matches the source’s two-page passage, while its minimal-polynomial terminology is left qualified. Exact missing propositionn°4 is not identified solely by its number.'
byid['CL-SA19-278']['present_status']='As of19November2026: the quotient-of-standard-étale theorem is established for unramified maps, and the standard-étale local presentation is established for étale maps. Neither gives unramified=>flat or a global primitive-element theorem over arbitrary finite fields.'
byid['CL-SA19-278']['confidence']='high for the exact local theorems; medium for the source minimal-polynomial convention'

